  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $4.9B in federal contract spending in FY2026 to date. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Treasury obligated $4.9B across 6,995 awards, with an average award size of $704K. Obligations fell 42.4% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show Treasury obligations of $9.6B in FY21, $9.3B in FY22, $10.3B in FY23, $9.3B in FY24, $8.6B in FY25, and $4.9B in FY26. Nonferrous metal smelting and refining is the largest spending category in FY2026 to date at $1.1B, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $962M and Computer Systems Design Services at $461M. STONEX FINANCIAL LTD is the largest vendor in FY2026 to date at $922M. The top 10 vendor list also includes ASAHI REFINING USA INC at $404M, FCN, INC. at $197M, and others. The figures reflect where Treasury is concentrating obligations so far this fiscal year and the vendors capturing the largest shares of those obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How large are Treasury's FY2026 contract obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $4.9B in FY2026 to date. Treasury awarded 6,995 contracts with an average award size of $704K, and obligations fell 42.4% year over year. Fiscal-year totals show a decline from prior years, with FY25 at $8.6B and FY26 at $4.9B so far."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Treasury's biggest procurement categories and top vendors?",
        "body": "Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining is the largest FY2026 category at $1.1B, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $962M and Computer Systems Design Services at $461M. STONEX FINANCIAL LTD is the largest vendor at $922M, and ASAHI REFINING USA INC is second at $404M, with other top vendors including FCN, INC. at $197M and WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC at $167M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of the Treasury spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $4.9B on contracts in FY2026 to date. Treasury recorded 6,995 awards in FY2026 to date and an average award size of $704K. Obligations fell 42.4% year over year, and prior fiscal years were $9.6B in FY21, $9.3B in FY22, $10.3B in FY23, $9.3B in FY24, and $8.6B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Treasury buy?",
      "a": "Treasury buys a mix of metals processing, IT services, and support services. Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining accounts for $1.1B in FY2026 to date, Other Computer Related Services accounts for $962M, and Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $461M, with additional purchases in metal rolling, custom programming, and warehousing."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Treasury's largest contractors?",
      "a": "STONEX FINANCIAL LTD is Treasury's largest contractor at $922M in FY2026 to date. ASAHI REFINING USA INC is second at $404M, FCN, INC. is third at $197M, and other top vendors include WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC at $167M and CRANE & CO., INC. at $146M."
    }
